WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.270
Let’s start off with a difficult question:
How do you define “reality?”

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.220
What is truly, “real?”

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.760
Is it simply a case of what we can see?

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:16.090
If something is known, as fact, and can be
proven to exist, does this make it real?

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:21.230
Is reality just the world around us, or is
there something more?

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:25.140
The goal of these questions isn’t to make
you question every part of the world around

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:29.360
you, or to question whether or not we are
all living in a computer simulation.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:35.040
No, you’re asked this to help you understand
reality, because first of all, we aren’t

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.480
living in a simulation… we’re living in
a sitcom.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:44.350
There is a wide ranging debate on what the
most powerful and dangerous SCPs ever encountered

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:50.320
are, but there is no denying the ever-present
danger of SCP-3812.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.400
This Keter-class entity is regarded as highly
aggressive by the O5 Council, especially as

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:00.120
it has only ever been partially contained,
never fully.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.089
The true scope of its abilities is currently
unknown, and any available information on

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:09.529
SCP-3812 is kept classified and secure by
the Foundation.

00:01:09.529 --> 00:01:15.850
Needless to say, this entity poses a direct
threat not only to the SCP Foundation, but

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.500
to the very fabric of reality itself.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.369
Contained within the file for SCP-3812 is
an excerpt from an article by one Doctor Robert

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:29.419
Scranton titled "Supersession and the Echelon
of Reality.”

00:01:29.419 --> 00:01:34.579
In this article, Doctor Scranton posits a
theory about the nature of reality, and understanding

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:37.729
him is the first step towards understanding
SCP-3812.

00:01:37.729 --> 00:01:43.730
His ”Recursive Stack” theory states that
there are different layers to reality, but

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:47.079
also that no single universe is “real.”

00:01:47.079 --> 00:01:52.899
An easy way to think of it is to imagine a
sitcom, any sitcom you can envision will do.

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:58.409
Between us, and the fictional world of a sitcom,
there are multiple observable stacked universes.

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:03.979
Firstly, our universe, the ”real world”
as we experience it, forms the baseline, so

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:06.450
imagine this sitting at the top of the stack.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:11.269
Next down in the stack comes the sitcom, a
fictional universe filled with characters,

00:02:11.269 --> 00:02:13.599
which fits below our universe.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:19.120
Then, think of what is fiction within the
fiction of the sitcom, perhaps another television

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.069
show, one that only exists in the world of
the sitcom, but not in our own.

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:29.579
This is the Recursive Stack, infinitely layered
universes, and it is crucial you can envision

00:02:29.579 --> 00:02:31.769
and remember this model.

00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:36.400
Doctor Scranton’s theory suggests that any
universe, even our own, could potentially

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.989
exist as a fictional narrative within another,
wider universe.

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:45.799
This wider universe, in which ours is a fiction,
could also itself be a narrative within an

00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:49.140
even wider universe stacked above it, and
so on.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.469
It’s interesting to picture reality this
way, isn’t it?

00:02:52.469 --> 00:02:56.330
In fact, I’m willing to bet that you’re
wondering, maybe there’s a universe above

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.540
ours, or even one above that.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:02.609
Would the universe right at the top of the
stack be the truly “real” world?

00:03:02.609 --> 00:03:06.099
And what if you could travel between each
stacked reality?

00:03:06.099 --> 00:03:11.530
If you are asking any of those questions,
then congratulations, you sound exactly like

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.530
SCP-3812.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:17.920
SCP-3812 was previously known as Sam Howell.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.900
While little is known about his life, Sam
was, as far as anyone knew, regarded as a

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.430
fairly ordinary human being.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:31.639
Until his death in 1996, shortly after which
Sam rose from his grave and disappeared.

00:03:31.639 --> 00:03:37.909
It is unknown whether SCP-3812 simply imitated
the form of Sam Howell, or if they are one

00:03:37.909 --> 00:03:43.440
and the same, as this entity has been known
to have the ability to change forms at will,

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.940
making it hard for the Foundation to track
it.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:50.629
It does usually maintain a humanoid appearance,
however this has deteriorated somewhat over

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:52.359
numerous decades.

00:03:52.359 --> 00:03:57.239
By now, you may have already gathered that
the extent of SCP-3812’s abilities don’t

00:03:57.239 --> 00:03:58.870
end at shape shifting.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:03.749
This SCP is a powerful, aggressive, reality
altering entity.

00:04:03.749 --> 00:04:06.620
Cast your mind back to the Recursive Stack.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:12.230
SCP-3812 is able to travel upwards through
these stacked universes, creating untold chaos

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.719
using its plethora of world-bending abilities.

00:04:15.719 --> 00:04:20.949
As far as the SCP Foundation can tell, 3812’s
sole intention is to become an omnipotent

00:04:20.949 --> 00:04:24.810
force existing above any and all possible
universes.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:28.490
In other words, the top of the stack.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:34.310
Aside from the ability to change shape, SCP-3812’s
control and alteration of a reality around

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:38.120
it is achieved by its long list of latent
abilities.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.600
This entity is capable of feats far beyond
that of normal humans such as teleportation,

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.600
telekinesis, telepathy.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:52.030
However, SCP-3812 is also able to directly
manipulate any and all aspects of reality.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:57.400
It can influence and alter observable forces
around us, for example the manipulation of

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:02.490
matter, energy, weather, and even gravity
and other Laws of Physics as we know them.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:05.590
But the creature can also warp reality on
further levels.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:11.230
It’s able to erase people, objects or even
concepts to the point where human beings lose

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:13.490
virtually all memory of them.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:18.370
With the danger that an entity this powerful
poses to our reality, it’s not surprising

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:22.539
that the SCP Foundation would attempt to nullify
its abilities.

00:05:22.539 --> 00:05:27.930
One attempt by the Foundation involved another,
unknown SCP which created an anti-metaphysical

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:28.930
field.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:34.210
This was done in the hopes that this would
strip SCP-3812 of its reality warping abilities,

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:39.460
however the entity was unfazed, the containment
attempt failed, and the remains of the unknown

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:44.740
SCP instead resulted in the creation of SCP-239.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:51.000
As for the SCP-3812 entity’s own origin,
that is still largely unknown.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:56.600
But there does exist a message on a secure
server in the SCP Foundation’s O5 Command,

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:01.919
seemingly from another entity belonging to
a reality stacked higher above our own, that

00:06:01.919 --> 00:06:08.139
appears to have created a reality much further
down, one that SCP-3812 inhabited.

00:06:08.139 --> 00:06:12.849
And now it seems that SCP-3812 is climbing
up the stack.

00:06:12.849 --> 00:06:18.180
There is a trade-off of sorts to the abundance
of powers SCP-3812 possesses.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:22.980
The entity is in an almost constant state
of ascension through different stacked universes,

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:27.400
climbing higher and higher, believing every
reality beneath it to be a fiction.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:31.550
The creature has developed multiple, severe
mental conditions that seem to be a direct

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:35.310
result of overexposure to different layers
of reality.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:40.460
This includes an advanced form of Eigenmann-Veitor
schizophrenia complex, which often manifests

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.370
in extreme symptoms within the creature.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:49.740
SCP-3812 has been known to suffer from paranoia,
dysphoria, depression, an inability to control

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:56.090
its emotions, as well as hearing voices, seeing
things that do not exist and possessing multiple

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.090
personalities.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:07:02.560
While the creature is usually aimless, SCP-3812
has been known to have random outbursts that

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.919
can cause anomalies within local space and
time.

00:07:05.919 --> 00:07:10.960
But, thanks to it experiencing so many different
layers of reality, traveling upwards through

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:17.070
what it perceives to be fictional universes,
SCP-3812 displays difficulty in separating

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:20.120
what is real, and what is imagined.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:26.050
In fact, reality and fiction have become one
and the same to SCP-3812, because as far as

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:29.740
it is concerned, they literally are the same.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:34.330
Each new reality it inhabits is just fiction
for the reality stacked above it.

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:38.360
So then how are we supposed to contain or
neutralize such a powerful reality altering

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.669
creature that cannot distinguish between what
is real and what is fictional?

00:07:42.669 --> 00:07:48.520
The Foundation knows that its own procedures
to keep SCP-3812 contained would be ineffective.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:52.210
This entity, by its nature, cannot be contained.

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:56.900
Any attempt to keep it locked away would easily
be undone by any one of its numerous powers

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.629
to warp reality.

00:07:58.629 --> 00:08:02.199
Locking it in a cement box at the bottom of
the ocean would be pointless.

00:08:02.199 --> 00:08:05.979
It could teleport out, or turn its cell into
nothing but dust.

00:08:05.979 --> 00:08:10.580
Putting it in a vat of acid to endlessly burn
it would just result in it turning that acid

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:13.169
to harmless water, or air.

00:08:13.169 --> 00:08:18.199
SCP-3812 can manipulate events throughout
time, and so it could easily prevent itself

00:08:18.199 --> 00:08:20.199
from ever being contained.

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:25.110
It is even possible that any individuals,
even Foundation staff, who may have previously

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:31.759
tried to luck the creature up, now no longer
exist thanks to SCP-3812’s abilities, and

00:08:31.759 --> 00:08:36.010
there would be no way to determine this since
we wouldn’t be able to remember that the

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:39.330
person had ever been in our reality.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:45.650
The Foundation’s best hope is to keep SCP-3812
where it is, and hope it remains docile.

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:50.820
If they are able to keep it away from large
population centers, then the risk of 3812

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:55.250
having any sort of psychic influence over
civilians, or warping reality and causing

00:08:55.250 --> 00:09:00.040
the deaths of millions or even billions, is
at least reduced.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.650
But of course it’s never fully gone.

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:08.230
On at least one occasion SCP-3812 has caused
a truly catastrophic event.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:14.130
For some reason, SCP-3812 decided to turn
itself into a star, spinning endlessly.

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:19.510
As it did so, numerous anomalous occurrences
took place across the world.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:25.930
Most notably, SCP-3812 caused the Foundation’s
nuclear warheads to detonate, spreading harmful,

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:28.450
radioactive material into the atmosphere.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:33.870
Additionally, the population of New Zealand
began to sporadically disappear and reappear,

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:38.530
looping back and forth between existence and
non-existence for a period of around five

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:39.530
hours.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:45.830
It was during this world ending scenario that
SCP-3812, still at the center of its star

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:49.850
form, was recorded ranting, its split personalities
arguing.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:54.260
One of the creature’s personalities claimed
it was “unmaking the world” as an act

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.110
of revenge against someone.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:59.430
It stated that it believed, “Existence is
a joke.

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:04.600
The narrative abandoned us to be miserable
and we are breaking the narrative.”

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:09.580
Its other half mentioned another entity, known
only as “Ben”, and seemed to imply that

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:15.340
this entity was responsible for SCP-3812’s
creation, in a reality stacked above this

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.340
one.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:21.220
According to the more rational of 3812’s
two halves, this ”Ben” entity “deemed

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.140
us unfit to rest peacefully.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.650
To slip into the darkness, quietly.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:27.600
He made a game of us.”

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.710
It then went on to convince its other half
that destroying this reality just to slight

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.510
Ben would be pointless.

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:36.510
There would always be another, stacked on
top, infinitely.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:40.150
“So why does this narrative mean anything
to you?”

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:41.150
it asked.

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:43.170
“It is one of an eternity of others.

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:44.500
It is not special.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.090
It is not particular.”

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:51.550
The two sides of SCP-3812 argued with each
other, one wanting to destroy all of reality

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:57.590
to spite Ben, driven mad by witnessing trillions
upon trillions of universes stacked atop each

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.590
other.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:04.370
The other half of 3812 saw peace for itself,
ascending above these infinitely stacked universes,

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.720
finally reaching the top and becoming free.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:08.400
“Not a god.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.270
A star, rising in the east.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:15.870
Rising away from this all until we are little
more than a memory of a song.”

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:19.120
“It will be lonely,” the other half of
the creature replied.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:23.060
“We’ll have each other,” SCP-3812’s
other personality said.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:26.070
“I’m afraid,” said the one intent on
destruction.

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:31.660
“I am too,” the other reassured it, “But
that is no reason to destroy this narrative.”

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:36.100
Eventually, SCP-3812’s personalities reached
agreement.

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:41.290
They both left the narrative they were currently
in, presumably traveling upwards to one stacked

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:45.550
above our own, while simultaneously remaining
in this universe.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.820
Still a danger.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:48.790
“Let go of this world.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:51.410
Let him rewrite it back to what it was.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:54.140
We aren’t part of this anymore.”

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:58.830
Shortly after this event, reality shifted
once more and the entire world reverted back

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:01.020
to how it had been before.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:05.380
Records of the end of the world scenario that
had occurred were retained by high-level administrators

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:10.950
and the O5 Council, perhaps as a reminder
of the destructive capabilities of the creature,

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:16.810
a warning of its potential to change this
reality and any stacked below or above it.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:23.170
Fortunately, since this incident, SCP-3812
has remained in its docile, aimless state,

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:26.390
no longer actively hostile to anyone that
approaches it.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:31.460
It has kept its amorphous, star-like shape,
and is still very much able to create disruptions

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:33.910
and anomalies in reality.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:39.030
Despite keeping SCP-3812 constantly monitored
at its current location in the South Pacific

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:44.990
Ocean, the SCP Foundation knows that, at any
time, this entity could trigger yet another

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:50.960
global catastrophe, causing massive damage
to planet Earth, its population, and beyond

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:53.940
that, tearing our reality itself asunder.

00:12:53.940 --> 00:13:01.550
So we all just better hope our narrative remains
worthwhile to SCP-3812’s better half...

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:08.950
Now check out “SCP-1861 - The Crew of the
HMS Wintersheimer” and “SCP-1765 - The

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:12.339
Sisters” for more reality-warping madness
from the SCP Foundation!

